{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/988166-expanded-duel-arcane-rules","id":988166,"title":"Expanded Duel Arcane rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T00:37:14-07:00","id":988166,"title":"Expanded Duel Arcane rules","content":"Since you were nice enough to visit the thread, here are some optional houserules for the 2E Duel Arcane. Let me know what you think!<br /> <br /> <b>Additional Doors: </b>Add +1 Door if losing would prevent you from fulfilling an Aspiration or Obsession. Add +1 Door if winning the duel would fulfill your Virtue or Vice. Add +1 Door if your Gnosis is higher than your opponent's. Add +2 Doors if your Gnosis is twice your opponent's. Subtract 1 Door if your opponent has a higher Arcanum rating than you (a Disciple versus an Adept, for example). Subtract 1 Door if your opponent is a Master and you are not. Subtract 1 Door if losing the duel would fulfill an Aspiration, Obsession, Virtue, or Vice.<br /> <br /> <b>Nimbus: </b>Duelists are affected by their opponent's Nimbus Tilt for the duration of the Duel Arcane. For example, if a mage's Nimbus gives -1 to Dexterity rolls, her opponent's Dexterity+Death attack would be penalized.<br /> <br /> <b>Edge: </b>Instead of Initiative, the Duel Arcane uses the Edge mechanic as a Chase would. Who has the Edge at a given time is based on the social context of the duel as well as the magical content of the clashing Imagos. The duelist with the Edge acts first in a given turn, and may optionally declare which Attribute category (Mental, Physical, or Social) will be rolled that turn. If it is unclear who has the Edge at the start of a turn based on the fiction, make a contested roll as per Chronicles of Darkness p.84. The Edge may be seized as described on p.85.<br /> <br /> <b>Called Shots: </b>You may take -2 on your Attack or Defense roll to inflict an [Attribute] Reduced Tilt on your opponent if your net successes exceed the chosen Attribute. Declare the Attribute being targeted before you roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>[Attribute] Reduced</b><br /> You have been denied your full abilities for the Duel. You take -2 on all Attack or Defense rolls in the Duel Arcane using the Attribute this Tilt applies to.<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt: </b>A successful Called Shot or an Exceptional Success from your opponent may inflict this Tilt, as can a Dramatic Failure from yourself.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt: </b>The Attribute reduction ends when the Duel Arcane ends. If it was inflicted by your opponent, they may lift it as a Negotiate option. </div> </div> </div><b>Conditions: </b>You may place a Condition on yourself or your opponent when you achieve an Exceptional Success, or have one placed on you by a Dramatic Failure. The following are some appropriate Conditions for the Duel Arcane. Conditions created by the Duel Arcane grant Arcane Beats when resolved (but only one per scene as usual), and fade when the Duel ends. If both parties choose to make the Duel more exciting, there is a +1 Reach effect for Display of Power that grants Exceptional Success on 3 successes rather than 5 for the Duration of the duel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Empowered</b><br /> Your connection to your Watchtower has been temporarily strengthened. Take an ongoing +1 to Attack or Defense rolls using your Path-derived Ruling Arcana. Resolve this Condition to increase this bonus to +3 for one roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Disrupted</b><br /> Your connection to your Watchtower has been temporarily weakened. Take an ongoing -2 to Attack or Defense rolls using your Path-derived Ruling Arcana. Resolve this Condition when you choose to fail a penalized roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Exposed</b><br /> You are especially vulnerable to the Inferior Arcanum of your Path. Attacks against you using your Inferior Arcanum gain +2 dice. Resolve this Condition by opening an additional Door when such an attack succeeds. [You should only use this Condition in Duels where your opponent has access to your Inferior Arcanum.]<br /> <br /> <b>Aggressive</b><br /> You have adopted an aggressive posture. Resolve this Condition to gain 8-again on one Attack roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Defensive</b><br /> You have adopted a defensive posture. Resolve this Condition to gain 8-again on one Defense roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Hesitant</b><br /> You doubt your own magical strength when on the attack. Take a -1 penalty and lose 10-again on Attack rolls. Resolve this Condition when you choose to fail a penalized roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Unbalanced</b><br /> You doubt your own magical strength when on the defense. Take a -1 penalty and lose 10-again on Defense rolls. Resolve this Condition when you choose to fail a penalized roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Baited</b><br /> Your opponent has taken the initiative and lured you into a trap. Take a -1 penalty on all Attack and Defense rolls. Resolve this Condition by allowing your opponent to choose whether you will Attack or Defend this turn. You choose what Attribute+Arcanum you will roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Centered</b><br /> You have found your calm in the middle of the storm. When you succeed on a Defense roll, you may resolve this Condition to close one of your own Doors. </div> </div> </div><b>New Merits</b><br /> <br /> Feel free to use these Merits as the basis for developing unique Style merits for the Duel Arcane.<br /> <br /> <b>Prepared Duelist</b> (\u2022)<br /> Your character is completely at home in the dueling ring. When she enters the Duel Arcane, she may choose one Condition to begin the duel with, such as Empowered or Aggressive. The Condition fades at the end of the duel if it has not been resolved already.<br /> <br /> <b>Precise Duelist </b>(\u2022)<br /> Your character knows exactly how to construct an Imago to draw out an opponent's weaknesses and nullify their strengths. Reduce penalties for a Called Shot in the Duel Arcane by one, and she need only match the opponent's Attribute, not exceed it.<br /> <br /> <b>Desperate Duelist </b>(\u2022)<br /> Your character throws himself into the clash of raw magical power, letting himself burn so long as his opponent scorches too. When he successfully opens a Door in the Duel Arcane, he may open one of his own Doors to immediately make a second Attack roll which the opponent may not Defend against. He may only do this once per turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Honorable </b>(\u2022)<br /> Your character is an old-school duelist, and his magnanimity catches more modernist opponents off guard. At the beginning of a duel, he may open one of his own Doors to inflict a Condition on his opponent, such as Baited or Shaken.<br /> <br /> <b>Underdog </b>(\u2022)<br /> Your character is very good at doubting his own abilities in a way that makes opponents drop their guard. At the beginning of a duel, he may choose to accept a Condition such as Disrupted or Swooned to immediately open two of his opponent's Doors.<br /> <br /> <b>Off-Hand Training</b> (\u2022)<br /> Your character has turned her weakness into a strength in the Duel Arcane. Choose one of her lowest Arcana. When using that Arcanum to Attack or Defend, she has +1 die and benefits from the 9-again property.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>The character loses this Merit if the chosen Arcanum ever has more dots than another Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <b>Impenetrable </b>(\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> Your character has 2 additional Doors in the Duel Arcane. Add +2 dice to any rolls to resist manipulation during or prior to a Duel, such as Negotiate attempts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-16-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:39:07-07:00","id":988167,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to talk about hacking the Duel Arcane rules with some ideas from 1E.<br /> <br /> First, some historical context for comparison. This is how the Duel Arcane worked in 1st Edition by default: The competitors begin the duel with an opposed Social roll, and the winner gets +1 dice to all attacks for the rest of the duel. Each competitor chose one Arcanum to be their Sword, and a different one to be their Shield. These Arcana were constant for the entire Duel. The Duel was run the same way as combat, attacking with Gnosis+Sword and subtracting the opponent's Shield as if it were their Defense. Willpower was treated as Health and lost from successful attacks, and when you ran out of Willpower points you lost. Just like Dodging, you could choose to forgo your attack for a turn to double your Shield/Defense, although there was little reason to do this beyond stalling for time if the Duel Arcane spell had a limited Duration, or you wanted to make your opponent waste precious Willpower getting past your defenses.<br /> <br /> The supplement Tome of the Mysteries provided a more in-depth discussion of dueling, some alternative forms of combat, and optional rules to make the core Duel Arcane more dynamic. Let's look at those rules, with a bit of sub-context first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Banishing Cycle</b><br /> Death&gt;Time&gt;Spirit&gt;Forces&gt;Mind&gt;Matter&gt;Fate&gt;Life&gt;Pri me&gt;Space&gt;Death...<br /> <br /> <b>The Invocation Cycle</b><br /> Prime&gt;Forces&gt;Fate&gt;Time&gt;Mind&gt;Space&gt;Spirit&gt;Life&gt;Deat h&gt;Matter&gt;Prime... </div> </div> </div>Optional rule 1: Once per turn, both duelists may change their Sword and/or Shield Arcana as a reflexive action. They both do this and reveal their choices at the same time.<br /> <br /> Optional rule 2: If your Sword is exactly one step above your opponent's Shield on the <i>Banishing Cycle</i>, you get +1 on your attack roll. If your Sword is below their Shield, you take -1 on your attack.<br /> If your Shield is exactly one step above your opponent's Sword on the <i>Invocation Cycle, </i>you get +1 Defense. If your Shield is below their Sword, you get -1 Defense.<br /> <br /> Optional rule 3: If your Sword and your Shield are next to each other on one of the two Cycles, you may choose one of the following two effects on your turn.<br /> <br /> If your Arcana have an <i>invoking </i>relationship: if you &quot;Dodge&quot; on your turn, you may reflexively roll Gnosis and regain 1 Willpower if you succeed.<br /> If your Arcana have a <i>banishing </i>relationship: you may forgo Defense for the turn to add your Shield to your attack roll.<br /> <br /> If you use either of these two effects, your weapons surge and dissipate and you must choose different Arcana for both your Sword and Shield next turn. On the turn after that, you can return to your originals if you want.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Now, back to 2E. The Duel Arcane works differently now, and resembles Social Maneuvering more than combat. I think a lot could be improved by drawing on the existing Social Maneuvering and Chase rules from 2E, but we may be able to mine some ideas from the 1E core and Tome of the Mysteries as well.<br /> <br /> <b>How can we best adapt the Banishing/Invocation Cycles to the 2E Duel Arcane? Do they only apply if a duelist chooses to Defend?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-16-2016, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T01:14:33-07:00","id":988177,"title":"","content":"Slight point of modification: The banishing cycle is not simply the invocation cycle run backwards, else the second optional rule is a functional non-change in 1e's mechanics.<br /> <br /> If memory serves there was a page on the now-defunct WoDIndex wiki that ran through the intended charting based on a clarification that resolved this contradiction, but the short version is that the banishing cycle runs through the Subtle Arcana in reverse order joined by the Gross Arcana that cross the ones neighboring those Subtle Arcana in the invocation cycle.<br /> <br /> i.e. Death &gt; Time &gt; Spirit &gt; Forces &gt; Mind &gt; Matter &gt; Fate &gt; Life &gt; Prime &gt; Space.<br /> <br /> The implications are slightly different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T05:59:26-07:00","id":988217,"title":"","content":"The only thing that comes to mind is that the Nimbus Tilt is not always a negative one (it can give bonuses) so maybe note that your oponent only gets affected by it if it is negative? Maybe you can get the bonuses yourself if it is beneficial, even if normally you can't be affected by your own Nimbus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T07:09:29-07:00","id":988236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/988166-expanded-duel-arcane-rules?p=988177#post988177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight point of modification: The banishing cycle is not simply the invocation cycle run backwards, else the second optional rule is a functional non-change in 1e's mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that makes significantly more sense. I noticed that the rules had weird implications by my reading but I couldn't figure out how else to read the bit in the 1E core about cycles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/988166-expanded-duel-arcane-rules?p=988217#post988217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that comes to mind is that the Nimbus Tilt is not always a negative one (it can give bonuses) so maybe note that your oponent only gets affected by it if it is negative? Maybe you can get the bonuses yourself if it is beneficial, even if normally you can't be affected by your own Nimbus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus it can affect Skills as well, which wouldn't apply in the Duel. I might strike that suggestion, I'm not sure there's a way to do it that wouldn't be too fiddly. Maybe an additional +1 Reach effect for Display of Power that both duelists can agree to apply, or an unscrupulous second can surprise one of them with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 10-16-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T08:12:31-07:00","id":988254,"title":"","content":"Here's a couple interpretations of how to use the banishing/invoking cycles.<br /> <br /> <b>Attack Bonus: </b>When the Arcanum you use to Attack is one step above or below your opponent's Defense Arcanum on the <i>banishing </i>cycle, you take a +1 bonus or -1 penalty respectively on your roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Defense Bonus: </b>When the Arcanum you use to Defend is one step above or below your opponent's Attack Arcanum on the <i>invoking </i>cycle, you take a +1 bonus or -1 penalty respectively on your roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Granting Conditions: </b>When you successfully Defend against an Attack using an Arcanum that <i>invokes </i>the attacking Arcanum, you may apply a beneficial Condition to yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>Inflicting Conditions: </b>When you successfully Attack past a Defense using an Arcanum that <i>banishes </i>the defending Arcanum, you may apply a negative Condition to your opponent.<br /> <br /> <b>Building Momentum: </b>When you successfully Attack, take a cumulative +1 bonus if your next roll uses the successive Arcanum on the <i>invoking </i>cycle. For example, Death is rolled normally, then Matter +1 is used to Attack, then Prime +2 is used to Defend. This bonus ends if you fail a roll.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T08:24:03-07:00","id":988255,"title":"","content":"While the <b>Negotiate</b> move is probably more dramatic and exciting if the concessions are outside of the dueling space, canny (or desperate) mages can offer terms within the Duel itself. These are often used when all of a duelist's Arcana have been blocked against a certain Door and they are forced to Negotiate to proceed. Here are some concessions a duelist might offer, mystically empowered by the dueling space:<ul><li>Cede the Initiative or the Edge to his opponent for the remainder of the Duel.</li> <li>Abstain from using a certain Attribute, or Attribute category for the desperate, for the remainder of the Duel.</li> <li>Abstain from using a certain Arcanum for the remainder of the duel.</li> <li>Grant his opponent a beneficial Condition and/or grant himself a negative Condition.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T09:57:53-07:00","id":988904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/988166-expanded-duel-arcane-rules?p=988177#post988177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If memory serves there was a page on the now-defunct WoDIndex wiki</div> </div> </div> </div>I summarized and clarified the expanded rules as presented in Tome of Mysteries on the Mage wiki, which is archived at the link below due to Wikispaces removing their free tier. The Duel Arcane reference starts on p50, but the formatting isn't great in the export.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-PosC1rNYUcRUYzZUVEZXdPUTA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-PosC1rNYUcRUYzZUVEZXdPUTA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-PosC1rNYUcRUYzZUVEZXdPUTA/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-PosC1rNYUcRUYzZUVEZXdPUTA/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11818-romzombie","name":"ROMzombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:07:29-07:00","id":988905,"title":"","content":"I can say for sure that if I ever end up running the duel arcane, I'm definitely going to use the Seizing the Edge mechanic now. <br /> <br /> All the other suggestions are also quite good, but I'd probably make all the Conditions into Tilts, especially with the enhanced focus on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T20:49:19-07:00","id":989176,"title":"","content":"I really like a lot of your ideas here. My goal for the Duel Arcane rules modifications would be to add more skill and tactics to it, so now that I've reviewed these I have greater appreciation for the potential role of tilts and conditions, new mechanics, etc.<br /> <br /> My only thought is that we don't need to bog down the mechanics too much. I probably would personally not want to use the optional rules for banishing/invoking cycle or Nimbus tilts, and I would probably condense and simplify some of the merits. Maybe make it more like a fighting style with multiple dots of increasing benefit?<br /> <br /> I'll review this before the next time we have a Duel in our PBP game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>My Games</b><br /> Mage 2E: The Supernal Suburbia (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/929924-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a> / <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/920977-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-the-supernal-suburbia\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>) - Storyteller","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8136-rwknoll","name":"rwknoll","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"785"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:45:33-07:00","id":989468,"title":"","content":"I got the canonical 1st-edition clarifications doc put onto the WoDCodex, for reference:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Duel_Arcane\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Duel_Arcane\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Duel_Arcane\" target=\"_blank\"> http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Duel_Arcane </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":